{
  "name": "How to Plan a New Interior Wall",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Planning a new interior partition wall? It's exciting to think about new layouts, but there are a few key steps to make sure it goes smoothly. First, mark out exactly where your wall will go on the floor. This lets you visualize the space and make any adjustments. Next, you'll want to lay out your plates and mark where each stud will sit. Don't eyeball this – precision is key for a straight wall! Now, here's a pro tip: measure your floor-to-ceiling height at several points along the wall and cut your studs to the shortest measurement. This helps avoid bowing if your ceiling isn't perfectly even. After that, you can assemble the frame right there on the floor. Once it's all together, you'll raise it into place, shim it until it's snug, and then fasten it securely, constantly checking that it's perfectly plumb. If you're dealing with tricky areas like existing structural framing or fire-rated assemblies, or if you're just unsure about the best way to handle your specific situation, it's a great idea to bring in experienced help like HH Remodeling. We've got the know-how to get it right the first time.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
